Expected elements: present

Every MUST-SHOW item is laid out and visible: fixed nav clear of the body, breadcrumb, hash with outcome badge, the `Not observable` card carrying the pruning reason and the permanence sentence, the affirmative provenance marker as the first `Data` row of the Overview grid (a row, not a band — exactly one marker on the page), all five content sections with their permanent-tense copy, and a footer that ends the page. No forbidden control, trace artefact, blame or danger tone. Nothing overflows, nothing clips, no horizontal page scroll: even the 66-character fee hex stays inside its cell.

Structurally the column holds a single left edge from the breadcrumb to the footer disclosure, and the provenance row does land before the empty sections. Two things spoil it. The column has two right edges: the Overview grid, the Decoded-input grid and the Raw block run to the column edge, while all five note cards stop about 210px short — so the page's most important block, the `Not observable` card, is also its narrowest. And section separation is not one system: Overview, Decoded input, Events and Raw each get a full-width rule and a large gap; Internal calls and State changes get neither, at roughly half that gap, though all six headings are the same level. The rule therefore asserts a group (Events + Internal calls + State changes) that the content contradicts — Events is about receipts, the other two about the trace.

Fix first: one right edge for cards and grids; one separator rule for peer sections.

Rating: 6/10

